rials\nCores & Initiatives\nResearch Clusters\nResearch Faculty\nHealth Sciences Graduate Programs\nMarshall Clinical Research Center\nMedical Student Research\nResearch Resources\nAt the Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine, biomedical research is a driving force behind innovation in patient care, medical education and community health. Our faculty, students and research teams are actively engaged in discoveries that advance our understanding of the molecular and cellular basis of disease and lead to improved treatments and outcomes.\nResearch Areas\nOur investigators explore a broad range of biomedical disciplines with strengths in the following fields that are of particular interest to West Virginia and other rural communities:\nCardiovascular disease\nNeuroscience and neurodegenerative diseases\nCancer biology\nObesity, diabetes and metabolic disorders\nSubstance use disorders and addiction\nAging and regenerative medicine\nRural and underserved health disparities\nTranslational Focus\nOur research programs emphasize collaboration between basic scientists and clinical investigators to accelerate the translation of laboratory findings into real-world applications. Through partnerships with Marshall Health Network and other regional institutions, we are committed to delivering research-driven solutions that meet the health needs of our Appalachian communities and beyond.\nTraining the Next Generation\nAs an R2 Carnegie-classified research institution, Marshall University is committed to developing the next generation of physician-scientists and biomedical investigators. Undergraduates through postdoctoral fellows benefit from immersive research experiences, dedicated mentorship and modern facilities through programs such as:\nHealth Sciences Graduate Programs\nMedical Student Research\nCores & Initiatives\nOur research infrastructure includes specialized centers, initiatives and core facilities designed to support high-impact investigations. Read More\nDriving Innovation for a Healthier Future\nThrough rigorous inquiry and a commitment to improving lives, biomedical research at the Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine plays a vital role in addressing today\u2019s most pressing health challenges. We invite you to explore our research, connect with our investigators, and join us in the pursuit of scientific advancement.\nABOUT US\nHistory\nNews\nMeet the Dean\nAccreditation\nEDUCATION\nMedical Education\nResidency Programs\nGraduate Medical Education\nContinuing Medical Education\nGraduate Education Programs\nRESEARCH\nCores & Initiatives\nBiomedical Sciences\nMarshall Journal of Medicine\nABOUT US\nEVENTS\nGIVE\n\u00a9 2025 Marshall University Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine\nWebsite Update Request | Site Disclaimer | Privacy Policy | Accreditation Statements", "links": [["GIVE", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/alumni-giving/giving/"], ["Current Students", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/"], ["Academic Portal", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/academic-portal/"], ["Services \u2794", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/research/"], ["Medical Education", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/medical-education/"], ["Academic Affairs", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/academic-affairs/"], ["Student Affairs", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/student-affairs/"], ["Academic Support", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/student-affairs/office-of-academic-support/"], ["Student Financial Assistance", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/financial-assistance/"], ["Medical Student Career Development Program", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/medical-student-career-development-program/"], ["Graphic Design Services", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/graphic-design-services/"], ["Specific Resources \u2794", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/research/"], ["MS-1 Students", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/ms-1-student-resources/"], ["MS-2 Students", "https://jcesom.marshall.edu/students/ms-2-student-